; The List datatype, declared from scratch.
;
; It is here — rather than pulled from the committed corpus — because this
; experiment's stores are all `mktemp -d`, so the registry and every client
; start with NOTHING. Two datatypes have to exist under exactly these names
; before anything else can be published: `Str`, because "…" surface literals
; elaborate to its constructors, and `List`, because the CLI entry shape the
; compiler recognises is (-> (List Str) Str) and it is matched against the
; CANONICAL List structure — Nil at index 0, Cons at index 1.
;
; So these two are published under BARE names, not under michael/*: a namespaced
; `michael/List` would not be found by either rule. That is a real constraint on
; what a namespace can hold, not an omission.
;
; Identity is structural, so this file is not a copy of the corpus in any sense
; that matters — putting it into an empty store reproduces the hash the committed
; corpus binds, and run.sh asserts exactly that against codebase/names.json.
(data List [a]
  (Nil)
  (Cons a (List a)))
